  "notes": [
    {
      "id": "note-dynamic-invocation",
      "reason": "FromDynamic binds a dynamic receiver; a dynamic invocation has no statically resolved symbol, so it must surface as binding incompleteness rather than an edge. The CoreApi.DynamicTarget() call in the same body is a normal Calls fact."
    },
    {
      "id": "note-with-clone",
      "reason": "'original with { Id = ... }' is lowered to the synthesized copy constructor/clone on ShapeRecord; the fixture records the property write (Writes -> ShapeRecord.Id) and the initializer call (Calls -> CoreApi.RecordTarget). Whether the lowered clone call also emits a fact is left to the Phase 7 mapping decision; the clone symbol is declared as M:CallShapes.Core.ShapeRecord.{Clone}$."
    },
    {
      "id": "note-collection-expression",
      "reason": "FromCollectionExpression returns [1, 2, 3]. Array types have no persisted symbol (no T:System.Int32[] row in the snapshot), so the array construction cannot be a persistable edge target; the construct is present for crash/incompleteness coverage."
    },
    {
      "id": "note-attribute-arguments",
      "reason": "C# requires attribute constructor arguments to be compile-time constants, so the only extractable fact in [ShapeMarker(19)] is the construction of ShapeMarkerAttribute."
    },
    {
      "id": "note-default-parameters",
      "reason": "C# requires default parameter values to be compile-time constants, so no call can occur in one. The fixture exercises the omitted-argument call shape instead (FromOmittedArgument calls OmittedArgumentTarget without passing its constant default)."
    },
    {
      "id": "note-csharp14-extension-block",
      "reason": "The call to the C# 14 extension block binds, in the current extractor, to a compiler-generated nested symbol (M:CallShapes.Core.ShapeTextExtensions.<G>$0A9D361FAFE148655B241EBC2970963E.BlockWordCount); the fact above records the callable extension member M:CallShapes.Core.ShapeTextExtensions.BlockWordCount(CallShapes.Core.ShapeText) as the intended target. The classic extension also gets an ExtensionReceiver edge today; the block form does not."
    },
    {
      "id": "note-partial-method-proof",
      "reason": "Measured on the committed fixture with the local Release build: the implementation part of a partial method is never walked, so no edge from OnShapePartial exists in the snapshot. The facts for OnShapePartial are the intended ones; the audit's Phase 7 extractor fix must make them appear."
    },
    {
      "id": "note-interpolated-handler-creation",
      "reason": "The interpolated-string-handler construction itself is compiler-lowered. Oracle C records the append calls (AppendLiteral/AppendFormatted) and the ShapeLog.Write call; it does not record a Constructs edge for the synthesized handler creation."
    },
    {
      "id": "note-measured-baseline",
      "reason": "Facts whose source is a body the current extractor already walks (classic extension, interface calls, local function, query lambda, async iterator, ref struct, unsafe, accessor bodies, static constructor, operator reads, type-level References) are copied from the measured snapshot; the C# 14 block-extension call is the one normalised exception. They are included so the Phase 7 exact-set test can diff the whole corpus rather than a subset."
    }
  ]
